NNOOTTEESS
       The  low-level  terminfo  interface is initialized using sseettuupptteerrmm(3X).
       The upper-level curses interface uses the low-level terminfo interface,
       internally.

PPOORRTTAABBIILLIITTYY
       X/Open Curses does not describe any of these except for ccuurr__tteerrmm.  (The
       inclusion of ccuurr__tteerrmm appears to be an oversight, since other  compara‐
       ble low-level information is omitted by X/Open).

       Other  implementations may have comparable variables.  Some implementa‐
       tions provide the variables in their libraries, but omit them from  the
       header files.

       All  implementations  which provide terminfo interfaces add definitions
       as described in the TTeerrmmiinnffoo NNaammeess section.  Most, but  not  all,  base
       the definition upon the ccuurr__tteerrmm variable.

